  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Wedding Website Options**\n\nI\'m currently evaluating the best technical approach for this wedding invitation website project. The user\'s preferences are clear: a modern, mobile-first design. I\'m focusing on either a NextJS (App Router) structure or a React setup with Tailwind CSS and a Supabase backend. I\'m leaning toward NextJS for its comprehensive features.\n\n\n**Assessing Project Environment**\n\nI\'ve got a much clearer picture now. It appears my environment is a Vite + React 19 + TypeScript SPA, with Express/Node available for backend tasks. The prompt defines the scope as a single-page application for a wedding invitation website. The requirement calls for sections: a hero section with a countdown, an \"Our Story\" timeline, an invitation with location details, embedded Google Maps, and a calendar integration.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Implementations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics. I\'m focusing on feature implementations. A gallery with a masonry grid and lightbox is essential. I\'m planning an RSVP form for guest details and a guestbook with real-time updates and liking functionality, with a fallback to local storage if Supabase credentials aren\'t set. Finally, an audio player and some light visual effects.\n\n\n**Prioritizing VietQR Integration**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing VietQR code integration for wedding gifts, recognizing its popularity in modern Vietnamese weddings. I\'ll need to figure out how to embed this functionality, likely as an additional section. In addition, I will create a modal or tab that makes Supabase configurations and schema DDL readily accessible for easy copying and pasting. I can also include instructions for deploying on Vercel and a clear folder structure for the project.\n\n\n"
