  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the Project Plan**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the project\'s architecture and constituent parts, as requested. I\'ve begun to sketch out the design. I\'m prioritizing the user\'s specific requests, including a hero section with the couple\'s names, wedding date, a nice background image, and a countdown timer. Next, I am thinking through the user\'s timeline request.\n\n\n**Developing Key Feature Sets**\n\nI\'m now implementing crucial feature sets. I\'m building out a section for key relationship milestones with images and brief descriptions. Next is the invitation with event details, Google Maps integration, and \"Add to Calendar\" features. I\'m also planning the photo gallery with a masonry grid and lightbox capabilities. Finally, I\'m developing the RSVP form and guestbook, integrated with Supabase for data storage.\n\n\n**Adding Vietnamese Features**\n\nI am now integrating requested Vietnamese wedding features. I\'m adding a \"Wedding Gift\" section with VietQR code and account details for both the bride and groom, which includes account number, bank and owner details, allowing a quick copy of the account number. I am adding a romantic audio background music player with play/pause, volume controls, and a vinyl disc aesthetic. Also, I\'m developing a toggleable effect for falling flower petals or hearts. I\'m adding a wedding card sharing option with a copy link and QR code. Finally, I\'m creating a modal with Supabase configuration instructions and the DDL SQL schema, for quick copy-pasting.\n\n\n\n**Defining the Database Schema**\n\nI\'m now formulating the database schema, including tables for RSVPs and the guestbook. I\'ve detailed fields like name, phone, attendance, and more for the RSVP table, alongside message, avatar color, and relationship for the guestbook. Also, I am thinking through Row Level Security (RLS) policies for both, allowing public inserts for RSVPs and reads/inserts for the guestbook, and updates on the likes_count. Next, I plan to develop `src/types/wedding.ts`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
