  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Header Wraps**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the first user request \342\200\223 the issue of header items wrapping on different screen widths. My analysis is underway, and I\'m zeroing in on the responsive design implications and potential CSS conflicts contributing to this line-break problem. I\'ll need to identify the breakpoints where the issue occurs.\n\n\n**Investigating Nav Layout**\n\nI\'ve been looking closely at the `Navbar.tsx` component. I\'ve broken it down into its three zones: brand, navigation links, and actions. I\'m thinking I\'ll need `whitespace-nowrap shrink-0` on nav links, and possibly adjust the container\'s max-width or spacing. Hiding text on smaller screens with responsive breakpoints, and ensuring no wrapping, is also key. On desktop, brand, links, and buttons should all be `whitespace-nowrap shrink-0`. I also have to test specifically between the md and xl screen sizes to check for collisions or wrapping.\n\n\n**Examining Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m checking the `package.json` file for the `motion` installation details. Next, I\'m shifting focus to the image gallery updates. I plan to revamp the image tabs in `Gallery.tsx` and `src/data/weddingData.ts`. It\'s time to streamline the gallery into three focused categories: \"T\341\272\245t C\341\272\243 \341\272\242nh,\" \"C\303\264 D\303\242u,\" and \"Ch\303\272 R\341\273\203.\" I\'ll curate photos for each section, featuring the bride, groom, and couple\'s images, while removing the other tabs.\n\nI\'m also paying close attention to the background image requirements for more vibrant sectioning, referencing the site `phan-anh-ngoc-yen.vercel.app` as inspiration, for rich, atmospheric backgrounds.\n\n\n"
