  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Layout Constraints**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on how specific CSS classes, particularly the combination of `max-w-6xl`, `mx-auto`, and `px-4`, influence text wrapping within the header. I\'m observing the behavior at different screen sizes, specifically between 768px and 1024px. I\'m honing in on how these classes work together with flex properties to produce the desired layouts.\n\n\n**Refining Wrapping Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining how text wraps in the navigation with specific constraints. Initially, I noticed the six nav items were wrapping because they lacked `whitespace-nowrap shrink-0`. This observation highlighted the layout\'s overflow behavior. I\'m now testing potential fixes like adding these classes or optimizing spacing, such as changing breakpoints to hide and display elements based on screen size. Additionally, I\'m simplifying the buttons in Zone 3 by showing icons, compact text, or \"RSVP\" to fit better.\n\n\n**Implementing Flexbox Fixes**\n\nI\'ve implemented `shrink-0` across all header containers to prevent unintended text wrapping or shrinking within the flexbox layout, which was causing inconsistencies. I also added `min-w-0` to the flex items using `items-center justify-between gap-2 sm:gap-4`, where appropriate, to allow for optimal shrinking without causing issues. I\'m now moving on to the implementation of the scroll-reveal effect for smooth section transitions, using IntersectionObserver, to improve the user experience.\n\n\n**Categorizing Image Assets**\n\nI\'m now cataloging beautiful photographs into distinct categories within `src/data/weddingData.ts`. I\'m meticulously sorting these into \'bride,\' \'groom,\' and \'couple\' subsets, aligning with the `src/types/wedding.ts` structure. I\'m making sure an \"all\" category displays all images when selected, allowing comprehensive browsing. Now I\'m preparing to implement engaging backgrounds for various sections as well.\n\n\n"
