    thinking: "**Analyzing Background Image**\n\nI\'ve been examining the background image implementation within `Hero.tsx`. Specifically, line 58 shows a background image with the id `photo-1519741497674-611481863552`. I\'m paying attention to the `div` elements applied to it, particularly the gradient overlaying. The gradient uses a mix of stone shades and transparency to create its effect. I\'m focusing on how these combine for the final look.\n\n\n**Revising Color Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the color palette to brighten the user interface. I\'ve pinpointed dark background elements in `index.html` and `App.tsx` contributing to the overall darkness. I also see dark color applications in `Hero.tsx` and countdown card with a `bg-stone-900/40`. I\'m starting from scratch with a palette of bright, warm ivory and pearlescent cream to give a joyful and energetic feel.\n\n\n**Defining Color Accents**\n\nI\'m now determining text, card, accent, and button color values to establish a vibrant, energetic visual language. I\'m focusing on elegant dark charcoal, warm rose, golden champagne, and vibrant emerald for text. For cards, a luminous white frosted glass effect will be created using `bg-white/92 backdrop-blur-md shadow-xl border border-rose-100/70`, coupled with soft warm shadows. Accents and buttons use a romantic coral rose gradient.\n\n**Visualizing Sectional Backgrounds**\n\nI\'m starting to generate background images for each section. For the hero section, I\'m thinking of a sun-drenched outdoor wedding photo with a radiant, blooming floral arch and blue sky, and a luminous scrim for the image. I\'m also considering a bright image with crisp white, gold, and text shadows, or a glowing pear.\n\n\n**Generating Sectional Images**\n\nI\'m now generating specific background images. For the Story section, I\'m leaning toward a bright garden scene with pastel flowers and sunbeams, using an overlay to enhance readability. The Invitation section\'s image will focus on a sunlit wedding ballroom with luxury accents, and a radiant letterhead design. The countdown timer will have bright numbers. I am still developing the gallery images.\n\n\n**Designing Sectional Visuals**\n\nI\'m now determining visuals for the RSVP, Guestbook, and GiftBox sections. I\'m drawn to a joyful pastel flower backdrop for photo cards. I envision a celebratory champagne toast for RSVP, and I\'m leaning toward wedding lights and confetti for the guestbook. For the giftbox, I\'m considering champagne with flower blossoms, and a warm rich rosewood or charcoal for the footer.\n\n\n"
